  "summary": "Darktrace reports an unattributed multi-stage ransomware intrusion (Sliver C2, Nmap scanning, DCSync via drsuapi::DRSGetNCChanges, PSExec/WMI/RDP lateral movement, SMBv1 encryption) with C2 to Vultr VPS 137.220.59.55 and data exfiltration to Wasabi cloud storage. The same page also documents CikaBika, a Rust RAT delivered by a Nim loader via a malicious LNK that stages a fake dbghelp.dll into Edge's directory through a ms-settings UAC bypass and uses Discord channels plus ngrok for C2 and exfiltration. Detection anchors include the Sliver JA3 d6828e30ab66774a91a96ae93be4ae4c, Sliver/Vultr and Wasabi endpoints, the %TEMP%\\IfyuUapz.txt payload path, the ms-settings registry hijack key, and the RAT's !shell/!download Discord command set.",
